                arabic: "وَجَآءُو عَلَىٰ قَمِيصِهِۦ بِدَمٍۢ كَذِبٍۢ ۚ قَالَ بَلْ سَوَّلَتْ لَكُمْ أَنفُسُكُمْ أَمْرًۭا ۖ فَصَبْرٌۭ جَمِيلٌۭ ۖ وَٱللَّهُ ٱلْمُسْتَعَانُ عَلَىٰ مَا تَصِفُونَ",
                translation: LocalizedText(en: "And they brought his shirt stained with false blood. He said, “Rather, your souls have enticed you to something. So beautiful patience. And God is the One whose help is sought against what you describe.”", ur: "And they brought his shirt stained with false blood. He said, “Rather, your souls have enticed you to something. So beautiful patience. And God is the One whose help is sought against what you describe.”", ar: ""),
                reference: "Yusuf · 12 : 18",
                reflection: LocalizedText(en: "The shirt is whole, untorn by any wolf, and Ya'qub knows at once. Yet he does not rage. He says sabrun jamil, beautiful patience. The Ahl al-Bayt defined it as patience that complains to no one but God. Not a heart that does not break - a grief carried to the right door.", ur: "The shirt is whole, untorn by any wolf, and Ya'qub knows at once. Yet he does not rage. He says sabrun jamil, beautiful patience. The Ahl al-Bayt defined it as patience that complains to no one but God. Not a heart that does not break - a grief carried to the right door.", ar: "The shirt is whole, untorn by any wolf, and Ya'qub knows at once. Yet he does not rage. He says sabrun jamil, beautiful patience. The Ahl al-Bayt defined it as patience that complains to no one but God. Not a heart that does not break - a grief carried to the right door.")
