            .narration(
                act: 3, tag: LocalizedText(en: "The Strength to Forgive", ur: "The Strength to Forgive", ar: "The Strength to Forgive"), source: LocalizedText(en: "Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq · Ilal al-Shara'i", ur: "Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq · Ilal al-Shara'i", ar: "Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq · Ilal al-Shara'i"),
                body: LocalizedText(en: "Standing at the height of his power over the very brothers who had thrown him into the well, Yusuf forgave them completely. Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq taught that this was not weakness but the highest form of strength - the strength to overcome the self's own hunger for revenge. The soul that once “commands to evil” is answered, at the last, by a mercy that asks nothing back.", ur: "Standing at the height of his power over the very brothers who had thrown him into the well, Yusuf forgave them completely. Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq taught that this was not weakness but the highest form of strength - the strength to overcome the self's own hunger for revenge. The soul that once “commands to evil” is answered, at the last, by a mercy that asks nothing back.", ar: "Standing at the height of his power over the very brothers who had thrown him into the well, Yusuf forgave them completely. Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq taught that this was not weakness but the highest form of strength - the strength to overcome the self's own hunger for revenge. The soul that once “commands to evil” is answered, at the last, by a mercy that asks nothing back."),
                reflection: LocalizedText(en: "To forgive from weakness is only to be unable to strike. To forgive from the throne - holding every power to punish, and setting it down - is the victory the whole surah has been climbing toward.", ur: "To forgive from weakness is only to be unable to strike. To forgive from the throne - holding every power to punish, and setting it down - is the victory the whole surah has been climbing toward.", ar: "To forgive from weakness is only to be unable to strike. To forgive from the throne - holding every power to punish, and setting it down - is the victory the whole surah has been climbing toward.")
            ),
